\section{Hash Function Selection: Keccak256 vs.\ Alternatives}

The choice of cryptographic hash function has direct implications for on-chain gas expenditure, security margin, and developer ecosystem compatibility. Five candidate algorithms were evaluated: MD5, SHA-256, SHA-3 (NIST), Blake2b, and the EVM-native \texttt{keccak256}. Table~\ref{tab:hash-comparison} summarises the comparison.

